  "summary": "SFPD disabled NCRIC and Western States Information Network access to its Flock ALPR network after an audit found 299 improper queries over about a year by out-of-state and federal agencies. Police said no ICE or DHS queries or immigration/reproductive-rights inquiries were identified, and that no federal agencies had direct access.",
  "key_quotes": [
    {
      "quote": "San Francisco police say they have disabled access to its network of Flock Automated License Plate Reader cameras after it was \"improperly queried\" for out-of-state and federal agencies.",
      "paragraph_idx": 6
    },
    {
      "quote": "There were 299 improper inquiries over approximately one year, which account for 0.005% of inquiries over that period",
      "paragraph_idx": 14
    },
    {
      "quote": "Upon discovering the improper searches, Chief Derrick Lew immediately turned off NCRIC's access to SFPD's ALPR system and initiated an internal review",
      "paragraph_idx": 16
    }
  ],
